    <string name="einr_betrieb_titel">When should Panoptes run?</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_text">“Always on” uses a little power from the battery and the 12 V battery while parked. Panoptes stops by itself before it gets low.</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_immer">Always on</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_immer_satz">Also when parked – needed for the Guardian.</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_fahrt">Only while driving</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_fahrt_satz">Saves power, but no Guardian while parked.</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_empfehlung">Recommended if you use the Guardian: Always on.</string>
    <string name="einr_betrieb_anpassen">You can change this later under Guardian → “Guardian stops when …”.</string>
    <string name="einr_stopp_akku" formatted="true">Battery below %1$s%%</string>
    <string name="einr_stopp_12v" formatted="true">12 V battery below %1$s V</string>
    <string name="einr_stopp_stunden" formatted="true">after %1$s hours parked</string>
    <string name="einr_karte_internet">The map needs internet.</string>
    <string name="einr_daten_titel">Data sharing</string>
    <string name="einr_daten_text">Everything is off. Only turn on what you want to share – you can turn it off any time under System → Data sharing.</string>
    <string name="einr_daten_keine">Panoptes does not know any data sharing options here yet.</string>
    <string name="einr_blitzer_aus">Leave off</string>
    <string name="einr_blitzer_an">Read – turn on</string>
    <string name="einr_updates_frage_pruefen">Should Panoptes look for updates?</string>
    <string name="einr_updates_pruefen_nein">You check yourself under System → App updates.</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_telegram_titel">Telegram</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_telegram_text">Messages from the Guardian and the car to your phone, via your own Telegram bot. Works over the internet, no extra program needed.</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_planer_titel">Connect the route planner</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_planer_text">Then you see on the road whether the battery lasts to your destination. You connect with a code on your phone.</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_cockpit_titel">Pair the EV Cockpit</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_cockpit_text">The EV Cockpit on your PC shows your car’s values. Pairing takes one tap.</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_fernzugang_titel">Remote access (Tailscale)</string>
    <string name="einr_extra_fernzugang_text">A direct path into the car over your own Tailscale network (free account needed). Only needed for: the web interface on a PC from elsewhere, live view and videos in full quality, remote maintenance (adb) and emergency access. For the phone app, “Connect your phone” is enough.</string>
